   "text": "The SMILES below was read region by region from the drawing.\n\n- **Isoquinoline core:** it carries NH2 at C8, F at C7, the pyridyl group at C6, and the amide NH at C3.\n- **Pyridyl substituent:** a pyridin-3-yl ring with a methyl at C4 and NH2 at C5.\n- **Linker:** from the isoquinoline NH, C(=O)CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013.\n- **tert-Leucine unit:** the C(=O)\u2013NH carbon is attached to a tert-butyl group and to the C(=O) that acylates the pyrrolidine nitrogen. Its stereocentre is drawn with a hashed bond.\n- **Hydroxyproline unit:** a pyrrolidine with a 4-hydroxy group (wedge) and a 2-carboxamide.\n- **Right-hand end:** the amide NH\u2013CH2 is attached to a para-phenylene ring bearing a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group.\n\nFor the stereocentres I matched the standard VHL-ligand configuration. I then checked the neighbour ordering and used @@ for the tert-leucine carbon in the way I wrote the SMILES, because swapping the order of the nitrogen and tert-butyl neighbours inverts the chirality symbol. I did not independently re-derive the CIP labels from the wedges and hashes.\n\nSMILES: Nc1c(F)c(-c2cncc(N)c2C)cc2cc(NC(=O)CCNC(=O)COCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N3C[C@H](O)C[C@H]3C(=O)NCc3ccc(cc3)-c3scnc3C)ncc12"
